        {
            "id": "note",
            "instance": "ab8bce91-a8c6-4976-9fdc-2c852feeee03",
            "properties": [
                [
                    "abstract",
                    "Detection of Program Protocol Sabotage & Malicious \"STOP\" Commands"
                ],
                [
                    "content",
                    "Tools like \"PLC_Controller\" can force Siemens controls into immediate \"STOP\" mode via ICS Protocols.\n\nHow does your network monitoring architecture log, alert, and differentiate deep process-level command mutations—such as a sudden native programmable logic controller (PLC) 'STOP' command sequence or rapid, repetitive Modbus register modifications—from a routine hardware or application failure?"
                ],
                [
                    "authors",
                    []
                ],
                [
                    "tags",
                    null
                ]
            ],
            "anchors": {
